{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387630-alternative-frailties-and-how-they-could-enchance-roleplay","id":1387630,"title":"Alternative frailties and how they could enchance roleplay","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-11T19:38:57-07:00","id":1387630,"title":"Alternative frailties and how they could enchance roleplay","content":"I was just browsing on reddit and saw a litle bit of discussion that was interesting, a user saying how he thinks pooka frailty do not really fits puca actual folklore. I Suggested to him &quot;why don't you make a rule where the pooka frailty changes depeding on it's legacy?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And Im thinking this might be a really interesting mechanic, what if every kith had a seelie frailty and a unseelie frailty?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Imagine the motley come to talk to a pooka npc and he says &quot;the baron is alive and well&quot; and suddenly all the PCs are worried about the Baron? Only to slowly realize the pooka is changing legacies at that time and don't need to lie anymore. This could even be weaponized by a crafty pooka. He could tell about the baron in a way to simulate his original frailty. This would add another layer to pooka lies, and another layer of roleplay to it, players would notice better, with suntle hints when a npc is changing legacies.<br /> <br /> <br /> If every kith had 2 frailties, one for each court, it could result in very interesting results, where this dynamic frailties affects the games in different ways. Many changelings also change legacies temporarily, without becoming of the other court.<br /> <br /> <br /> If all alternative frailties are planned well, the pooka situation could very well happen to all other kiths, making up for very interesting intrigue games. Is this boggan truly helping us, or is he feigning his frailty? Let's put him in a situation where his other frailty might appear, so we can be sure. Etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Also, it could be interesting if the player chooses which frailty belongs to which court, opposed to the frailties actually being seelie or unseelie. The same for NPC frailties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 05-11-2020, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T20:28:02-07:00","id":1387879,"title":"","content":"I definitely think it's an interesting concept and many kiths do have room to fit two story concepts together and operating with both of those as aspects in their mien.<br /> <br /> I definitely think it could be interesting as an optional rule but one that would be difficult for players to use given how long we've used the default form and all that. It's one of those things that kind of remind me of stuff like the mechanics you find in storyteller's guides or The Danse Macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T20:10:03-07:00","id":1388218,"title":"","content":"I Feel like your example is.. metagaming? Frailties shouldn't be known to a mechanical detail but vague understandings.. Trolls are honorable. Pooka stretch the truth, Boggans help the needy.. I don't think players should act on a mechanical understanding like &quot;oh a Pooka says something... we have to assume every word they say is a lie&quot; that just seems poor separation of mechanic from story.. it would be like saying &quot;that guy has strength 3&quot;<br /> <br /> That being said I think some variations in BR and frailty can add alot to character customization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T09:13:28-07:00","id":1388341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387630-alternative-frailties-and-how-they-could-enchance-roleplay?p=1388218#post1388218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Feel like your example is.. metagaming? Frailties shouldn't be known to a mechanical detail but vague understandings.. Trolls are honorable. Pooka stretch the truth, Boggans help the needy.. I don't think players should act on a mechanical understanding like &quot;oh a Pooka says something... we have to assume every word they say is a lie&quot; that just seems poor separation of mechanic from story.. it would be like saying &quot;that guy has strength 3&quot;<br /> <br /> That being said I think some variations in BR and frailty can add alot to character customization.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's a fair point, but while some frailties might be considered just like a common traits, others are surely seem as some kind of weakness or curse, like the sluagh, they don't all whispers just to mantain a mistery air around them. Also there are some legends about how some frailties came to be, which can be known by changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T16:19:03-07:00","id":1388476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387630-alternative-frailties-and-how-they-could-enchance-roleplay?p=1388341#post1388341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That's a fair point, but while some frailties might be considered just like a common traits, others are surely seem as some kind of weakness or curse, like the sluagh, they don't all whispers just to mantain a mistery air around them. Also there are some legends about how some frailties came to be, which can be known by changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some are more specific than others. Knowing that Pooka are prone to lies doesn't mean you know everything they say is a lie(and that's not even supported by c20). If every word out of a Pooka's mouth was a lie.. it would be predicatable.. Banal.. it makes the con harder. Players should always be guessing. That being said having greater versatility in frailties isn't a bad thing. Pooka are shapeshifing animal tricksters having other ways to manifest this than say &quot;cannot answer directly&quot; is an idea worth working with. Trolls are honorable.. there ae other ways to manifest it. Boggan take care of the home....<br /> <br /> But on the other hand you have the Sluagh and the Selkie. a Sluagh who isn't silent isn't really a Sluagh and a Selkie is defined by their coat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T20:24:32-07:00","id":1391118,"title":"","content":"I allow River Hags in my game, but replace their Frailty with River-Blooded: A River Hag that is not in a river treats damage as one type worse for the purposes of healing. This means a River Hag heals Bashing Damage on her sheet as though it were Lethal Damage, and Lethal Damage on her sheet as though it were Aggravated. A River Hag cannot heal Aggravated Damage on her sheet unless currently in a river.<br /> <br /> The rationale behind this houserule was that their baseline Frailty requires extreme anvil-tossing on the ST's part to pull off. &quot;Spend a week not in their home river and they DIE.&quot; Which, if the game involves travel, is unplayable. If it's a &quot;local&quot; game, the only way to invoke some &quot;captured by the bbeg&quot; plot device or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}